<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sahara</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Saharan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sahara is the largest hot desert in the world, covering most of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> from the Atlantic to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a>. Trans-Saharan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravan-trade">caravan routes</a> carried gold, salt, slaves, textiles and ideas between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>, sustaining empires on both sides of the desert. It is central to the profiles of the Garamantian, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanem-bornu-empire">Kanem-Bornu</a> and Almoravid empires, among many others.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sahara.jpg" alt="Sahara" width="320" height="173" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Project Apollo Archive · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sahara_real_color.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
